{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b3b14b10aa04511d","name":"card_unit_2_marine_division","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/NavalWarfare/units/card_unit_2_marine_division","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"2. MARINE DIVISION","text":"Once per turn, deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ when you play a Navy card.","flavorText":"The 2nd Marine Division of the German Kriegsmarine was formed in March 1945 in Schleswig-Holstein from excess naval personnel and hastily assembled troops. Most of its members were poorly trained and lacked combat experience, far from the standards of a regular army unit. The division was short on heavy weapons and relied mainly on small arms and panzerfausts. Key support elements, including engineer and supply units, were never fully established due to equipment shortages. Declared ready for action in early April, the division was rushed into the defense of the Weser-Aller line, south of Bremen. It engaged in scattered battles along the Aller River, notably at Verden and Rethem, losing all of its anti-aircraft batteries during the fighting. Casualties mounted rapidly under Allied pressure and by April 21, only 3,000 of the original 13,000 men remained. The remnants continued delaying actions near Cuxhaven and Meldorf, eventually falling back behind the Kaiser Wilhelm Canal. Reduced to a few hundred men, the unit acted as a local alarm force before surrendering to British troops at Bunsoh in early May 1945.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_2_marine_division","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_2_marine_division_title","SourceString":"2. MARINE DIVISION","LocalizedString":"2. MARINE DIVISION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_2_marine_division_text","SourceString":"Once per turn, deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ when you play a Navy card.","LocalizedString":"Once per turn, deal 3 damage to the enemy HQ when you play a Navy card."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_2_marine_division_history","SourceString":"The 2nd Marine Division of the German Kriegsmarine was formed in March 1945 in Schleswig-Holstein from excess naval personnel and hastily assembled troops. Most of its members were poorly trained and lacked combat experience, far from the standards of a regular army unit. The division was short on heavy weapons and relied mainly on small arms and panzerfausts. Key support elements, including engineer and supply units, were never fully established due to equipment shortages. Declared ready for action in early April, the division was rushed into the defense of the Weser-Aller line, south of Bremen. It engaged in scattered battles along the Aller River, notably at Verden and Rethem, losing all of its anti-aircraft batteries during the fighting. Casualties mounted rapidly under Allied pressure and by April 21, only 3,000 of the original 13,000 men remained. The remnants continued delaying actions near Cuxhaven and Meldorf, eventually falling back behind the Kaiser Wilhelm Canal. Reduced to a few hundred men, the unit acted as a local alarm force before surrendering to British troops at Bunsoh in early May 1945.","LocalizedString":"The 2nd Marine Division of the German Kriegsmarine was formed in March 1945 in Schleswig-Holstein from excess naval personnel and hastily assembled troops. Most of its members were poorly trained and lacked combat experience, far from the standards of a regular army unit. The division was short on heavy weapons and relied mainly on small arms and panzerfausts. Key support elements, including engineer and supply units, were never fully established due to equipment shortages. Declared ready for action in early April, the division was rushed into the defense of the Weser-Aller line, south of Bremen. It engaged in scattered battles along the Aller River, notably at Verden and Rethem, losing all of its anti-aircraft batteries during the fighting. Casualties mounted rapidly under Allied pressure and by April 21, only 3,000 of the original 13,000 men remained. The remnants continued delaying actions near Cuxhaven and Meldorf, eventually falling back behind the Kaiser Wilhelm Canal. Reduced to a few hundred men, the unit acted as a local alarm force before surrendering to British troops at Bunsoh in early May 1945."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnCounterMeasureTriggered","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/NavalWarfare/t_2_marine_division.t_2_marine_division","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Top","artist":"German WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/2__MARINE_DIVISION.2__MARINE_DIVISION","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":342.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_2_marine_division_photo","SourceString":"German Marines on the march. Date unknown.","LocalizedString":"German Marines on the march. Date unknown."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryL'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryL.47"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeHeavy_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeHeavy.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""},"threat_level":0.1},"variables":[{"name":"tmpCard","type":"i